\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Tanigaki: Reserves Should Be Held As  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Funds  \b0\par\par\uc2 195 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 08:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said Friday that the nation's massive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves should be held as they are now, ruling out the possibility of selling off any of its reserve holdings.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki, speaking before the Upper House Budget Committee, said that Japan's reserves have grown large as a result of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 's past yen-selling, dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But when asked if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had any plans to sell off its reserve assets, such as any of its U.S. Treasury holdings, Tanigaki said that it was best to hold the reserves as they are.  \par \par \uc2 'It is meaningful to keep holding our reserves, as they can be used as future \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  funding,' Tanigaki said, referring to reserves as necessary funding for any yen-buying, dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's government can finance yen-selling, dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  borrowing yen through the issuance of financing bills.  \par \par \uc2 But in the event it wants to conduct yen-buying, dollar-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's weakness, it must sell dollars held in its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves.  \par \par \uc2 -0-   \par \par \uc2