\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Mr Yen sees no yuan revaluation before 2007-paper.  \b0\par\par\uc2 380 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 04:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SEOUL, March 4 (Reuters) - China is unlikely to change its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system until 2007 at the earliest as it needs more time to prepare, former Japanese finance ministry official Eisuke Sakakibara was quoted as saying in a South Korean newspaper.  \par \par \uc2 Sakakibara, who became \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's front-man for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1995 to prop up a sagging dollar, earned the nickname "Mr Yen" for his influence on exchange rates in the late 1990s.  \par \par \uc2 "Be it a revaluation of the yuan or expanded trading band, it will take at least two years for China to prepare," the Chosun Ilbo on Friday quoted Sakakibara as saying in an interview.  \par \par \uc2 He also said the yen could break above 100 per dollar over the short run, but did not expect the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rally further to 90.  \par \par \uc2 The yen was quoted at 105.30/40 per dollar around midday in Asian trade on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 Sakakibara also said South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves, standing at more than $200 billion, were not excessive because the country would have to cope by itself if there was a repeat of the type of financial crisis experienced in the late 1990s.  \par \par \uc2 "South Korea needs to keep a considerable amount of reserves and $200 billion is not too much," he said.  \par \par \uc2 There has been some criticism from domestic media and politicians that South Korea was wasting taxpayer's money by holding an excessive amount of foreign reserves.  \par \par \uc2 South Korean reserves rose 24 percent to a record $202.16 billion by the end of February from a year earlier, according to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  data on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 In an attempt to earn more from the reserves, South Korea plans to set up a government agency to invest some of the reserves in higher-yielding assets, modelled after the Government of Singapore Investment Corp Pte Ltd.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, he said Japan and China had recently discussed forming an alliance to tackle turbulences in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, including putting about 5 percent of each country's foreign reserves under joint management.  \par \par \uc2 Japan, China, South Korea and Taiwan together hold about $2 trillion in reserves, which have resulted from years of heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and soaring trade surpluses.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050304e134001b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
