\par\par \b \uc2 Japan  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  account not hurt by unrealised losses-MOF.  \b0\par\par\uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2005\par 09:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Feb 23 (Reuters) - The health of a special account that holds \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets acquired through \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is not hurt by its unrealised losses, a \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MOF) official said on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Massive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past have racked up unrealised losses in the budget's special account over the last few years. The losses are expected to rise to around 11.4 trillion yen ($109.5 billion) by the end of March next year.  \par \par \uc2 But Kiyoto Ido, head of the ministry's international bureau, told a parliamentary committee that such losses will not be realised unless the ministry sells all the foreign assets held in its international reserves, or sell dollars for yen.  \par \par \uc2 "Given the current situation, that is not something we can imagine," Ido said.  \par \par \uc2 Ido said foreign assets in the ministry's international reserves are held in case of a possible need for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and it was important for the ministry to continue holding them in foreign-\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  denominated assets.  \par \par \uc2 "Even if there are unrealised losses in yen, it won't immediately have an impact on the management of the special account."  \par \par \uc2 He said Japan's foreign reserves have been making profits through its reserve management due to lower interest rates in Japan compared with other countries.  \par \par \uc2 "We are making profits through reserves (portfolio) management and they (the losses) are not worsening the balance in the special account and not causing problems to the health of the account," he added.  \par \par \uc2 Japan has had the world's largest foreign reserves for more than five years. At the end of January the reserves stood at $840.966 billion, of which $696.978 billion was in securities and $124.225 billion in cash. The rest includes IMF reserve positions and gold.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is financed by borrowing yen by selling short-term government paper, whose yields are much lower than yields of foreign securities, such as U.S. Treasuries, that Tokyo buys for its foreign reserves.  \par \par \uc2 The major factor causing an increase in unrealised looses in the special account is the yen's rise against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 When calculating losses in yen for the latest budget documents, the MOF used a revised projection for a dollar rate of 109 yen, compared with 115 yen a year earlier and 121 yen two years ago. The dollar was around 104.80 yen on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities sold a record 20 trillion yen ($192 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2003 and another 15 trillion yen in the first three months of 2004 in an attempt to halt what they saw as an excessive rise in the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Ido said the ministry conducted \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2003 and early 2004 to prevent speculative and excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements from hurting the Japanese economy, and such a move had a positive effect on the economy.  \par \par \uc2 "At that time, there were geopolitical risks such as the situation in Iraq and excessive attention was given to the U.S. twin deficits. Although the U.S. economy was fundamentally strong, there was strong speculative dollar selling and we took action against it.  \par \par \uc2 "As a result, we were able to prevent excessive \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements from having a negative impact on corporations and consumer sentiment," Ido said. ($1=104.15 Yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050223e12n006q0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
