\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Ex-MOF Mizoguchi sees no change in G7  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  stance.  \b0\par\par\uc2 521 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Januar 2005\par 09:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  TOKYO, Jan 27 (Reuters) - Major industrial powers are expected to maintain their previous appeal for less-volatile \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets and greater flexibility in exchange rates in a meeting next week, Japan's former top financial diplomat Zembei Mizoguchi said on Thursday.   \par \par \uc2  Mizoguchi, vice finance minister for international affairs until last June, also told a group of reporters that any decline in the dollar on concerns about U.S. trade and budget deficits was not likely to be very deep. "I do not believe that the bottom for any decline in the dollar will be that deep," said Mizoguchi, currently head of the Japan Center for International Finance, a government-affiliated research body.   \par \par \uc2  "The (U.S.) twin deficits are not problems that warrant immediate concern, although over the medium to long term, both budget and current account deficits should be reduced," he said.   \par \par \uc2  Concerns over huge U.S. trade and budget deficits have pushed the dollar to five-year lows against the yen and to all-time lows against the euro in recent months, causing worries in Japan and Europe about the potential damage to their exports.   \par \par \uc2  But Mizoguchi said finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs from the Group of Seven industrial nations meeting in London next week would probably repeat the G7's stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  used at a meeting last February in Boca Raton, Florida.   \par \par \uc2  The statement had said that excess volatility and disorderly movements in exchange rates were undesirable for economic growth and that the G7 wanted more flexible exchange rate systems in all trading zones of the world.   \par \par \uc2  "There are trade imbalances, but it's not something that needs to be quickly adjusted through \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates," Mizoguchi said.   \par \par \uc2  "Conditions have not changed, so I don't believe the G7 is in a situation where they have to change the wording (of the statement)," he said.   \par \par \uc2  With China also set to join the meeting, Mizoguchi said he expected some discussion on how and when the country would revalue its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , fixed at about 8.28 to the dollar.   \par \par \uc2  But he said Beijing would likely take its time.   \par \par \uc2  "A radical change in China's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy will probably take more time," he said.   \par \par \uc2  "The focus is on whether they take any steps before that out of consideration for international concerns," he said.   \par \par \uc2  Japanese businesses have mixed feelings about a yuan revaluation because while China is a trading rival, many use it as a manufacturing base and as a market for exporting consumer goods.   \par \par \uc2  Japanese officials also want to give Beijing more time to decide how and when to change \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy without disrupting its economy and markets.   \par \par \uc2  Analysts also say a revaluation of the yuan could fuel a rally in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the yen, but Mizoguchi declined to comment on whether he believed the yen would appreciate.   \par \par \uc2  During his term at the Finance Ministry, Mizoguchi oversaw mammoth \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in which \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a record 35 trillion yen ($339 billion) over 15 months to slow a sharp appreciation of the yen. ($1=103.13 yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050127e11r008hz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
