\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar firm on US rates outlook, yen falls.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Natsuko Waki  \par \uc2 668 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2005\par 13:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 21 (Reuters) - The dollar hit a 1-1/2 week high versus a broadly weak yen on Friday, underpinned by expectations for higher U.S. interest rates and fading speculation Asian authorities would let their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise soon.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback drew support from comments by Federal Reserve officials hinting they could accelerate the pace of interest rate hikes. Fed officials assured the market on Thursday the bank stood ready to act on inflation and more Fed speakers are due later on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The yen slipped as jitters grew about possible Japanese yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fading expectations the Group of Seven rich nations will succeed in convincing Asia to share the burden of dollar weakness when they meet next month.  \par \par \uc2 "In general, the cyclical factor is working in favour of the dollar, especially the interest rate environment," said Steven Pearson, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at HBOS Treasury Services.  \par \par \uc2 "Asia is generally weak because the market is losing confidence Asia will let their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  go. The volume of comments from (Japanese) Finance Ministry officials has stepped up as well."  \par \par \uc2 By 1230 GMT the dollar had risen two thirds of a percent to a 1-1/2 week high of 103.91 yen. The euro was up half a percent at 134.61 yen.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was steady at $1.2964, within half a cent of two-month lows hit on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Sterling tumbled after UK retail sales for December showed an unexpected month-on-month decline in the Christmas shopping period. The decline in sales was the most rapid for the month of December since 1981.  \par \par \uc2 FED TALKING UP  \par \par \uc2 On Thursday, San Francisco Fed President Janet Yellen said the Fed had sent its members out with "trumpets and megaphones" to warn of higher interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 St. Louis Fed President William Poole also said the bank was ready to move aggressively to pre-empt inflation.  \par \par \uc2 Higher interest rates support a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by making deposit returns more attractive to global investors. Later on Friday, Fed board governor Susan Schmidt Bies and Minneapolis Fed President Gary Stern are due to speak.  \par \par \uc2 "Fed officials are taking every opportunity to tell the market that U.S. interest rates still have some way to rise," said Adrian Foster, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein.  \par \par \uc2 The prospect of higher interest rates has helped the dollar make a strong recovery in 2005 after falling for three years due to the dollar's low-yield status and worries over the U.S. current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 NO BURDEN SHARING?  \par \par \uc2 In the run up to the London G7 meeting in February, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials have been urging Asia to let their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rise to share the burden of dollar weakness.  \par \par \uc2 Germany's government said on Friday it was "increasingly worried" by the euro's high exchange rate against the dollar, according to a draft economic report obtained by Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 The report also urged other world countries to play their part to tackle the causes of the dollar weakness and said that the burden should not and must not fall only on the euro zone.  \par \par \uc2 The yen rose to a five-year high of 101.65 per dollar this week, raising concerns about possible yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki reiterated on Friday \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would act in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market if needed.  \par \par \uc2 The G7 meeting will be attended by key emerging economies including China - which has come under international pressure to revalue its pegged yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The view Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will rise sharply after the G7 meeting may not materialise, analysts say.  \par \par \uc2 "I think few people seriously think there will be drastic changes in global \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy after the G7 meeting," said Etsuko Yamashita, chief economist at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corp.  \par \par \uc2 Later in the day, the University of Michigan's consumer confidence index, due at 1445 GMT, is expected to show a rise to 98.0 in January from 97.1 in December.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050121e11l00d1p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
