\par\par \b \uc2 Dollar maintains gains, focus on US rates, flows.  \b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2005\par 08:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Jan 20 (Reuters) - The dollar maintained gains near the previous session's two-month high against the euro on Thursday, underpinned by the view the United States could accelerate the pace of raising interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 It also drew support from speculation U.S. multinational companies may repatriate their funds to take advantage of a tax break.  \par \par \uc2 Drugmaker Johnson & Johnson (JNJ.N) said on Wednesday that it would repatriate about $11 billion in past earnings, while rival Pfizer Inc (PFE.N) said it was considering repatriating up to $38 billion.  \par \par \uc2 Markets are awaiting an inaugural speech by U.S. President George W. Bush due later in the day. His administration has pledged it would tackle the U.S. budget deficit - one of the factors behind the dollar's three-year weakness.  \par \par \uc2 The focus was also on speeches by Federal Reserve officials, including St Louis Fed's William Poole and San Francisco Fed's Janet Yellen.  \par \par \uc2 By 0741 GMT the dollar was steady at $1.2993 per euro , close to a two-month high of $1.2962 set on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was slightly lower against the yen at 102.62 .  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was torn between speculation for higher Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of a Group of Seven meeting next month and jitters of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by Japanese authorities.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  repeatedly warned this week it would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, even solo, if it was necessary.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese vice finance minister Koichi Hosokawa holds a news conference later.  \par \par \uc2 Elsewhere, European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet and Vice President Lucas Papademos hold press briefing.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050120e11k008kg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
