\par\par \b \uc2 =DJ UPDATE: Japan Policy-Makers Worry  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Could Hurt Econ  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 874 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2005\par 00:45\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japan's government Wednesday warned for the first time in 10 months in its monthly economic report that the yen's recent gains could hurt the economy, while policy-makers chorused their concerns about the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market has been unstable and he would watch closely for any impact on the economy.  \par \par \uc2 He told a regular news conference that Group of Seven finance ministers and central bankers at a meeting Feb. 4-5 in London would 'more strongly confirm' their view that disorderly moves aren't welcome and exchange rates should reflect fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 The government's report and comments from policy-makers follow gains in the yen against the dollar and other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week. The dollar touched a five-year low of Y101.67 Monday, while the euro Wednesday fell to a four-month low of Y132.99.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki wouldn't comment on recent \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates but threatened to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in markets to stop the yen's rise. 'We need to monitor the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market closely, and are ready to take proper action against excessive moves,' he said.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets since it ended in March last year a 15-month campaign to cap the yen.  \par \par \uc2 Yen Has Gained Against Dollar, Euro  \par \par \uc2 A stronger yen would further depress already sluggish exports and hurt industrial production.  \par \par \uc2 With that possibility in mind, both the government and Bank of Japan left unchanged their cautious assessment of the economy in monthly reports, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy board said in reviewing forecasts it issued last October that economic activity is slightly weaker than it had expected.  \par \par \uc2 'The economic recovery has been moderating recently, with some parts of the economy showing weakness,' the Cabinet Office said in its report.  \par \par \uc2 While the economic recovery is expected to progress firmly in line with a global recovery, 'there's a need to be mindful of such things as inventory adjustments in information-related sectors and trends in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates and crude oil prices.'  \par \par \uc2 It was the first time since April last year that the government report explicitly mentioned \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates as a risk factor.  \par \par \uc2 'We need to monitor \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate movements carefully,' a Cabinet Office official briefing reporters on the economic report said. 'Since January, the yen has appreciated not only against the dollar but also against the euro. Even when viewed through the broad picture of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates, the yen is strong.'  \par \par \uc2 Fukui Expects G7 To Warn On \b \highlight22\uc2 Forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  The yen's gains have in part been prompted by expectations that European and U.S. officials might increase pressure on Asian countries to strengthen their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the G7 meeting to ease global trade imbalances.  \par \par \uc2 Fukui said that those at the meeting will 'no doubt' discuss global imbalances, likely referring to the U.S.' large current account and budget deficits.  \par \par \uc2 'Recent \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves have been somewhat unstable,' he said.  \par \par \uc2 Fukui made the comments at a press conference after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's board voted unanimously to keep monetary policy steady in Japan.  \par \par \uc2 In its monthly report, the BOJ reiterated that 'Japan's economy continues in a recovery trend, although there seem to be somewhat weak movements mainly in production.'  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ last October forecast that real gross domestic product would grow by 3.6% this fiscal year ending March 31 and 2.5% next fiscal year. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't issue new forecasts for GDP but did note a change in the method of calculating GDP introduced by the government last November. The change led to a cut in previous GDP estimates.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ said that taking into account the new method, policy board members' forecasts for real GDP growth could be translated to around 2.5% for this fiscal year and 1.5% for next fiscal year.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last October also forecast that the core CPI would fall by 0.2% this fiscal year but rise 0.1% next fiscal year, which would satisfy one of the BOJ's conditions for ending its quantitative easing.  \par \par \uc2 Consumer prices 'are also expected to be basically in line' with last October's forecasts. But due to a a reduction in telephone charges, consumer prices 'may deviate slightly below' the BOJ's forecasts, it said.  \par \par \uc2 The government repeated its view that exports, production and consumption are either weak or growing at a slower pace.  \par \par \uc2 It maintained its assessment that industrial production 'is weakening.' In addition to moderating overseas demand for Japan-made goods, Japanese manufacturers' increased efforts to reduce inventories of digital parts and devices have weighed on output, it said.  \par \par \uc2 Exports are still weakening while imports are 'leveling off,' the government said. But it downgraded its assessment of Japan's surplus of trade in goods and services, saying the surplus is moderately decreasing instead of saying it is 'flat.'  \par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com (Hiroshi Inoue, Leika Kihara, Takeshi Takeuchi and Asako Tanabe contributed to this article.)  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Hugh Lawson  \par \par \uc2 -0-  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050504e11k00b71\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
