\par\par \b \uc2 Fukui says G7 to seek stable  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 , balanced trade.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Chisa Fujioka  \par \uc2 703 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2005\par 11:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Jan 19 (Reuters) - Caught between calls for more flexibility in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and worries about a higher yen, Japan said on Wednesday the Group of Seven will address both global imbalances and \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability at their upcoming meeting.  \par \par \uc2 Although Europe's calls for Asia to shoulder a bigger share of the burden in easing the bulging U.S. current account deficit have fuelled speculation Tokyo would be forced to refrain from market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Toshihiko Fukui stressed that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stability was a top priority for the G7.  \par \par \uc2 He complained that exchange rates had become unstable lately and ought to reflect economic fundamentals, referring to the yen's gains of about 10 percent against the dollar in the last three months to five-year highs.  \par \par \uc2 "As it is the start of the year, we will discuss the outlook for the global economy as well as long-term imbalances," he told a news conference when asked about the agenda for the meeting of G7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs on Feb. 4-5.  \par \par \uc2 "For the time being it's necessary to secure a more sustainable recovery this year and next year," he added, however. He noted that the G7 had repeatedly stated that volatile exchange rate movements were undesirable.  \par \par \uc2 Japan conducted a record 20 trillion yen ($195.7 billion) in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2003 to halt the yen's rise and spent a further 15 trillion in the first three months of last year. However, its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  campaign suddenly stopped in mid-March amid widespread criticism from its trade partners.  \par \par \uc2 The yen is now up more than 30 percent against the dollar from its troughs of three years ago. After hitting a five-year high of 101.67 to the dollar on Monday, it was hovering near 102.30 on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 A higher yen makes Japanese products less competitive on the global markets, which would be a major setback for the country's export-reliant economy struggling to emerge from more than a decade of stagnation.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  SPECULATION  \par \par \uc2 Fear of a revival of Tokyo's heavy \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  has played a part in slowing the yen's rise against the dollar, compared with the euro's rally. China's policy of pegging its yuan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar has also dampened an appreciation in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in general.  \par \par \uc2 But European officials, including European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet, have this month urged Asian countries to share more of the burden of recent dollar weakness.  \par \par \uc2 This has sparked market speculation that the G7 talks would focus on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility, stepping up pressure on China to revalue the yuan.  \par \par \uc2 But Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki warned on Wednesday that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could not be ruled out, saying \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would act if it saw abnormal moves in exchange rates.  \par \par \uc2 "I think we need to carefully monitor recent movements. If there are abnormal movements we need to take necessary action," Tanigaki told a regular news conference.  \par \par \uc2 The yen barely moved on the remarks, but the market understood what he meant.  \par \par \uc2 "The main message was this: don't discount \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the domestic economy falters," said Naomi Fink, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at BNP Paribas in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 Economics Minister Heizo Takenaka said the yen's recent rise was not very large in real effective exchange rate terms - a way of gauging the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's broader value against those of Japan's major trade partners and inflation rates in those countries - but that the speed of the rise was a concern.  \par \par \uc2 "It has not risen that much in real effective exchange rate terms. However, the rate of change is also important and we will closely monitor that," Takenaka told a news conference.  \par \par \uc2 The yen's real effective exchange rate index, compiled by the BOJ, has yet to reach its peaks hit a year ago, standing at 120.2 in mid-December, down from 120.4 in November and around 124 in early 2004.  \par \par \uc2 Most \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analysts believe the G7 at its February meeting will stick to a phrase they have repeatedly used in their recent statements calling for both flexibility and stability. ($1=102.17 Yen).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050119e11j00c1f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
