\par\par \b \uc2 Yen seen lagging any yuan revaluation rally in Asia.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By David McMahon  \par \uc2 852 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Januar 2005\par 06:52\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Jan 19 (Reuters) - The yen, which climbed near a nine-year high against the dollar this week on speculation that China may soon revalue its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , is seen lagging any rally in other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  when Beijing eventually moves.  \par \par \uc2 Expectations of a relaxing of the yuan's peg to the dollar are to some extent already factored into the heavily traded Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which many investors have used as a proxy to bet on an across-the-board rise in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Any sharp rise in the yen could also see \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  order yen selling by the Bank of Japan (BOJ) to stamp it out, analysts say.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar/yen would probably have less room to move since a revaluation by China would likely force the BOJ out of hiding," says Ashley Davies, a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist for UBS in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 The yen has already risen 28 percent against the dollar since January 2002, while the yuan has been virtually pegged at 8.276 to 8.28 yuan to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese authorities have made no secret of their displeasure about the impact of a further sharp rise in the yen on the country's export-reliant economy.  \par \par \uc2 Other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are set to rise in unison, as central banks across the region remove pegs to the dollar or gradually give up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the rise of free-floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Davies, who expects China to relax the yuan from its peg to the dollar by two percent in the first half of this year, said a revival of yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ would likely help the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hold above 100 to the dollar this year.  \par \par \uc2 He sees the Taiwan dollar as the biggest winner in a yuan revaluation, due to its close trade ties with China and a strong economy.  \par \par \uc2 INITIAL REACTION  \par \par \uc2 Most analysts see a revaluation of the yuan as early as this month or as late as a year from now, through a widening of its narrow band against the dollar to 2 to 5 percent in the first of several moves towards a free float.  \par \par \uc2 China has come under increasing pressure, especially from the United States, to let the yuan float against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  - a move that could ease pressure on the huge U.S. trade deficit.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  shot up to a five-year high against the dollar of 101.67 yen on Monday, riding on comments last week by European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials that Asia should bear a greater share of the burden of exchange rate adjustments.  \par \par \uc2 Until now the euro has borne the brunt of the dollar's decline, gaining almost 50 percent against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since the start of 2002, almost double the yen's gains.  \par \par \uc2 On Wednesday the euro was at $1.3030 The yen was around 102.40 though traders see it creeping back towards 101.25 yen, a level last seen in December 1995.  \par \par \uc2 Tomoko Fujii, director of economic and market analysis for Nikko Citigroup in Tokyo, said she was sceptical of the argument that a stronger yuan would trigger massive \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the BOJ, but she said an initial overshoot in the yen was unlikely.  \par \par \uc2 "To some extent the yen has already reacted over the past few days after ECB officials raised the need for burden sharing," she said.  \par \par \uc2 Nevertheless, Fujii said the yen would gain from such a move in the longer term and likely end this year at 95 to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Nikko Citigroup expects China to move the yuan to a trading band of 2-3 percent in a "limited revaluation" within 3-6 months.  \par \par \uc2 Many analysts say that in the longer term Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will grow more comfortable with allowing a stronger yen, because if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Japan's Asian rivals gain in tandem, it exports will remain competitive in global markets.  \par \par \uc2 EXTREME SCENARIO On the extreme side, some argue that China may wait as long as a year to move on its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and then surprise the market with a one-off revaluation of a much larger magnitude.  \par \par \uc2 "I think if China goes, they're going to have to go big," said Harvinder Kalirai, head of Asia-Pacific research and analysis at State Street. "And I'm talking like 20 percent."  \par \par \uc2 "The other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  wouldn't be moving 20 percent overnight, but over the course of a year we'd see pretty significant appreciations of something like 10 to 15 percent."  \par \par \uc2 Kalirai said China may choose this option since a small widening of the trading band would only invite the inflow of hot money as speculators bet on further revaluations.  \par \par \uc2 In the meantime, traders said yen-proxy trades were set to continue as speculation buzzes about a more flexible yuan.  \par \par \uc2 "The easy option is to trade what you can, and that's euro yen," said Luke Waddington, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading at Royal Bank of Scotland in Tokyo. "I think we're going to see some exaggerated moves."   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050119e11j006sh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
