\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF says would conduct solo  \highlight22\uc2 fx intervention \highlight\uc2 .  \b0\par\par\uc2 314 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Januar 2005\par 13:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Jan 18 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is ready to act alone in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stem the yen's rise against the dollar, a senior Finance Ministry official said on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 The yen rose to a five-year high against the dollar on Monday after European officials said Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  needed to take on more of the burden of the dollar's decline, while the euro continued to ease against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Asked about \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  following the remarks by European officials, the ministry official told Reuters: "If necessary, we are ready to conduct solo \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."  \par \par \uc2 On Monday, the dollar touched 101.67 yen , its lowest level since January 2000.  \par \par \uc2 When the dollar fell against both the euro and yen late last year there was speculation in financial markets that Japanese and European authorities would act together to boost the dollar to help protect exports.  \par \par \uc2 Following the latest comments by European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials including ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet, traders had wondered whether Japan would be willing to act alone.  \par \par \uc2 At 1145 GMT, the dollar was trading near 102.70 yen. Earlier on Tuesday, it hit a two-month high against the euro as market attention swung back to rising U.S. interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that while the dollar may continue to gain against the euro, the yen would likely remain well supported ahead of a meeting of Group of Seven finance ministers in early February.  \par \par \uc2 Many traders expect G7 nations to repeat calls for Asian countries to adopt more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  regimes, which would be taken by the market as putting pressure on China to allow its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise by relaxing its peg to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Such a rise would likely buoy other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the yen, given strong economic ties in the region.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050118e11i00dnr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
