\par\par \b \uc2 CORRECTED - CORRECTED-JGBs rally across board, supported on Nikkei, yen.  \b0\par\par\uc2 658 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Januar 2005\par 08:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In TOKYO story headlined "JGBs rally across board, supported\par  on Nikkei, yen" please read in eighth paragraph ....a record high\par  of 99.910.... instead of ....99.910 percent (correcting to\par  clarify the figure is not a percent).\par      A corrected story follows.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 By Kazunori Takada  \f28 \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Jan 18 (Reuters) - Japanese government bond prices rallied across the board on Tuesday, recovering the previous day's losses, helped by sluggish Tokyo shares and worries that the yen's recent strength could damage the export-led recovery.  \par \par \uc2 On Monday, the yen rose to a five-year high of 101.67 per dollar and its highest level since September versus the euro amid calls from European authorities for more \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  flexibility in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 "The market confirmed there was little downside room after government-related funds were detected bargain-hunting around 1.4 percent," said Seiji Shiraishi, chief market economist at Daiwa Securities SMBC, referring to the cash benchmark 10-year yield.  \par \par \uc2 "That and the yen are aiding the bond market today."  \par \par \uc2 At 0602 GMT, the yield on the benchmark 266th 10-year cash bond was down 3.0 basis points at 1.360 percent while the 20-year yield was also down 3.0 basis points at 2.005 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The five-year yield was down 2.0 basis points at 0.555 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The key March JGB futures contract ended the session up 0.26 point at 139.16.  \par \par \uc2 At the shorter end of the market, key June 2005 three-month euroyen futures briefly hit a record high of 99.910 , helped by strength in the JGB market.  \par \par \uc2 The contract was at 99.905, up 0.005 point at 0623 GMT, indicating a rate of 0.095 percent in June.  \par \par \uc2 "There is no change in the market's view about the economy. Players are just buying back futures after selling them on machinery orders data," said a money trader at a U.S. brokerage.  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei share average closed down 0.56 percent at 11,423.26.  \par \par \uc2 JGBs SUPPORTED ON YEN  \par \par \uc2 Although the yen retreated to around 102.50 yen on Tuesday, traders said ongoing pressure from European and U.S. officials wanting to see the appreciation of Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , notably the Chinese yuan, would keep the yen on a rising trend.  \par \par \uc2 "It looks like joint \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  between \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Europe is unlikely. Even if \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  alone, you can't expect it to have too much effect on the market," said Daiwa's Shiraishi.  \par \par \uc2 Following Friday's surprisingly strong Japanese machinery orders data for November, the key JGB futures contract shed half a point while the 10-year yield rose 5.0 basis points to 1.4 percent.  \par \par \uc2 But prices are now back at levels prior to the machinery orders data.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the market appears to have confirmed the 1.4 percent level as a ceiling for 10-year bonds for now, and looks set to bring yields further down.  \par \par \uc2 "Cash bonds are firm, taking futures prices higher, as pensions and other investors are seen shopping across the curve, particularly from medium to super-long maturities," said Hiroyuki Kubota, a Fisco bond analyst.  \par \par \uc2 An auction of 1.3 trillion yen ($12.71 billion) of 15-year floating rate bonds on Tuesday produced firm results, as expected, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  offering them at a 101 basis point discount to the base rate.  \par \par \uc2 The base rate for the initial coupon payment is 1.39 percent.  \par \par \uc2 On Thursday, the ministry will auction 600 billion yen of 20-year JGBs, and traders will carefully watch the result to determine if the market can absorb longer-dated issues given recent low yields and a mixed economic outlook.  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan kicked off a two-day policy meeting on Tuesday at which it is expected to keep its current ultra-loose monetary policy unchanged. ($1=102.24 Yen) (Additional reporting by Chikako Mogi).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050118e11i0070w\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
