\par\par \b \uc2 Tanigaki: Will Act If  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  Doesn't Reflect Fundamentals  \b0\par\par\uc2 464 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2005\par 02:25\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Current \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  movements require careful monitoring, Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said Monday, vowing to act in markets if movements stray from economic fundamentals.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "As is written in the communiques issued by the Group of Seven (industrialized nations), we believe \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates should move stably in reflection of fundamentals," Tanigaki said after the dollar fell to a five-year low of Y101.81 on Friday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 "If movements stray from fundamentals, we will take proper action," he said. [ 17-01-05 0146GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki, who had been visiting the Philippines and India last week, said he noticed that \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets had moved while he was away. "The current situation is one which requires very careful monitoring."  \par \par \uc2 But he declined to answer a question on whether it would be difficult for \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the next meeting of G7 finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors in London on Feb. 4-5, repeating only that Tokyo will act if \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements become unruly.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki also said that the focus for adjusting global imbalances should be on structural reforms, when asked whether he thought \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  adjustments were an effective way to address such imbalances.  \par \par \uc2 "Not only \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  systems, but the state of a nation's economy and finances are at issue," Tanigaki said. "Looking at the big picture, structural reform efforts should take center stage" when dealing with global imbalances.  \par \par \uc2 He added that structural reform efforts, which include maintaining fiscal discipline, will vary according to each country.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki was speaking after European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Chief Economist Otmar Issing said earlier this month that Europe is absorbing an unfairly heavy share of the dollar's broad weakness. Issing called on Asian nations, namely China, to start contributing to reducing global imbalances stemming from the large U.S. current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 The Japanese finance minister also said he hoped to increase the share of non-Japanese investors' holdings of Japanese government bonds, which currently stands at 4%.  \par \par \uc2 While declining to give a specific numerical target, Tanigaki pointed out that the ratio of foreign ownership of government bonds in other countries was significantly higher - around 24% for the U.S., 12% for the U.K. and 40% for Germany.  \par \par \uc2 This week, the Japanese government will hold its first-ever roadshow to pitch JGBs to investors from the U.S. and Europe. As its budget deficit continues to grow, Tokyo is working to attract new types of investors into JGBs to help absorb the record amount of government bonds that will hit the market during the next several years.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Bennett Richardson and Chris Gallagher [ 17-01-05 0220GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050117e11h00015\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
