\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Japan \highlight\uc2  MOF: No  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  From Nov 27 To Dec 28  \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2004\par 11:00\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  authorities stayed out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for most of December, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday, marking the ninth consecutive month of inaction.  \par \par \uc2 The Ministry said it didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market from Nov. 27 to Dec. 28 despite the U.S. dollar's slide to near five-year lows during the month.  \par \par \uc2 Investor concerns over the U.S. current account and budget deficits have continued to pressure the dollar, driving it down to a low of Y101.83 on Dec. 2, its lowest level since December 1999. [ 30-12-04 1006GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 The Ministry has stayed out of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since mid-March, when it abruptly ended an unprecedented 15-month yen-selling campaign to hold down the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 If the Ministry doesn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  till the end of the year, that total \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  for 2004 would amount to Y14.83 trillion, all of which was carried out between January and March.  \par \par \uc2 Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  data cover trades that are settled in December. Spot \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trades are settled after two business days.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the ministry's continued lack of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki had said Tuesday that there is a growing view that U.S. and European speculators may take advantage of thin year-end trades to test the greenback's downside again.  \par \par \uc2 "At the end of the year and the start of the new year, we must closely watch how \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves play out," Tanigaki had said, suggesting that authorities stand ready to act again if the need arises.  \par \par \uc2 -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Ven Ram [ 30-12-04 1020GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041230e0cu00080\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
