\par\par \b \uc2 Euro hits new record high vs yen in thin trade.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Chikako Mogi  \par \uc2 530 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 Dezember 2004\par 03:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Dec 30 (Reuters) - The euro scaled an all-time high against the yen on Thursday, with the market betting on further euro strength against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on deep-rooted worries about the U.S. trade and budget deficits.  \par \par \uc2 With the new year approaching, traders and investors were looking for the dollar to extend its roughly three-year decline against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to the swelling and record U.S. current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 "Although it looks as if it's the euro's day, what's driving the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher is not fundamentals in the euro zone but structural problems in the United States," said Shogo Nagaya, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Nomura Trust and Banking.  \par \par \uc2 "The dollar is expected to face fresh selling pressures across the board at the start of the new year," he said.  \par \par \uc2 Exchange rates were choppy in thin volume as Thursday marks the last trading session of 2004 for Tokyo dealers. Traders said volatility was likely to pick up closer to the start of London trade.  \par \par \uc2 The euro hit an all-time high of 141.59 yen according to data from electronic trading platform EBS. It was up from 141.31 yen in late New York trading.  \par \par \uc2 Just a day earlier, the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a record high against the dollar for the fifth straight trading session at $1.3647, according to EBS.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said that after speculators and investors had taken profits on the euro's gains to record highs they were renewing bets for the euro to climb further against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "It looks like profit-taking in the euro had come full circle and players started building fresh long positions in euro/yen," said Kaoru Kondo, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at financial data provider Fisco.  \par \par \uc2 Traders had expected volatility to rise sharply around the Japanese commercial fixing at 0100 GMT, and demand from banks for euros gave momentum to its early jump against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 At 0155 GMT, the euro bought around $1.3595 slightly off $1.3606 in late New York and down 0.4 percent from its all-time peak.  \par \par \uc2 With the euro rising to fresh highs versus the yen, the selling of the yen against other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped to keep the dollar firmly supported against the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was up at 104.10 yen from 103.86 yen in late New York.  \par \par \uc2 But some traders saw current euro/yen levels to be nearing a peak, and a corrective fall in euro/yen could push the dollar back down to its five-year low of 101.83 yen hit on Dec. 2, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Kondo at Fisco said euro/dollar faced option orders between $1.3650 and $1.3700, which could limit the euro's rises versus the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 This year has seen the dollar fall around 4 percent against the yen and nearly 8 percent versus both the euro and the British pound.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will release monthly data on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  at 7 p.m. (1000 GMT), with traders expecting it to confirm that no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was conducted in December.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041230e0cu002bd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
