\par\par \b \uc2 Germany Schroeder For Veto Rts For New UN Council Members  \b0\par\par\uc2 558 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2004\par 08:31\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (AP)--New permanent members of an expanded U.N. Security Council should have the same veto rights as those who currently hold seats, German Chancellor Gerhard Schroeder said Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Speaking at an economic forum during a trip to Japan, Schroeder said "double standards shouldn't be applied" if the Security Council were enlarged.  \par \par \uc2 Germany and Japan are both lobbying, together with Brazil and India, to win permanent seats on the U.N. body. Though Tokyo has long insisted that nations joining Britain, China, France, Russia and the U.S. should be awarded a veto, this is the first time Schroeder has mentioned the issue.  \par \par \uc2 New members should have equal status, Schroeder said in response to a question about veto rights after he gave a speech to the forum.  \par \par \uc2 "That means of course that they, like the (permanent five), should have the veto right," he said.  \par \par \uc2 An international panel on Nov. 30 proposed two options to expand the Security Council from the current 15 members to 24 members. But neither option would add any new veto-wielding members.  \par \par \uc2 One proposal from the panel would add six new permanent members - two from Asia, two from Africa, one from the Americas and one from Europe - as well as three non-permanent members elected for two-year terms.  \par \par \uc2 The other proposal would create a new tier of eight semi-permanent members chosen for four-year terms - two each from Asia, Africa, Europe and the Americas. It would also add one non-permanent seat.  \par \par \uc2 Schroeder added he hoped that two African nations would join Brazil, Germany, India and Japan in their campaign.  \par \par \uc2 "I hope that we can invite two countries from the African continent to this initiative," he said.  \par \par \uc2 On global oil prices, the chancellor said he hoped there would be better means to ascertain demand for oil from the economies of China and India to stabilize prices, adding he hoped the Group of Eight countries would cooperate to boost market transparency.  \par \par \uc2 "I think the time has come that the G8 states take a common initiative for more transparency on the oil markets. I will soon make such proposals to my colleagues," Schroeder said without elaborating.  \par \par \uc2 "We think that with more transparency in key price influences, for example the demand situation in China and India, we must remove the basis for speculation."  \par \par \uc2 The chancellor briefly weighed in on \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  during his address, though avoided specifics about the U.S. dollar, which has fallen sharply against the yen and euro over the past two years.  \par \par \uc2 "I know about the independence of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But one hint I want to give is one can sometimes learn something from Japan and his excellent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies," Schroeder said.  \par \par \uc2 He didn't elaborate, though Tokyo is known for actively selling yen for dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to keep its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from rapidly appreciating. A weak dollar hurts Japanese exporters by lowering the value of their overseas earnings when converted back into yen.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market since March, however, when it wound up a months-long multibillion dollar campaign to keep the yen from strengthening.  \par \par \uc2 In the January-March quarter alone, Japan spent Y14.83 trillion ($142 billion) buying dollars on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. [ 09-12-04 0731GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041209e0c9000do\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
