\par\par \b \uc2 Corporate losses may spur new Asian  \highlight22\uc2 FX intervention \highlight\uc2 .   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Rajat Bhattacharya   \par \uc2 828 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Dezember 2004\par 08:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Dec 9 (Reuters) - Fujio Cho ought to be a troubled man these days.   \par \par \uc2 The president of Toyota Motor Corp., the world's largest automaker by market value, complained in November that it would be "troublesome" for Japanese companies if the dollar were to drop below 105 yen.   \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to a five-year low of 101.83 yen last week and has traded below 105 yen since Nov. 17, cutting Toyota's earnings from exports when converted to yen and contributing to a 5 percent drop in its shares in the past month.   \par \par \uc2 Lee Kun-hee, who heads Asia's most valuable electronics company, Samsung Electronics Co. Ltd., should be worried as well.   \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won has surged almost 9 percent in the past two months, darkening Samsung's profit outlook and triggering a 13 percent drop in its shares. The company derives four-fifths of its revenues outside South Korea.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts are watching to see if the influence of powerful businessmen such as Cho and Lee will persuade the region's authorities to step up their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and start buying dollars to protect the profits of its biggest firms.   \par \par \uc2 "The government in Korea will get into trouble with the large conglomerates if they allow the won to appreciate further," said Ashley Davies, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS in Singapore, predicting increased \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of Korea before the end of the year if the won appreciates towards 1,000.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Thursday that the gain in the won, which was around 1,055 per dollar, had been excessive. It reached a seven-year high of 1,037 on Monday.   \par \par \uc2 "PSYCHOLOGICAL WAR"   \par \par \uc2 Asian central banks, holding an estimated 70 percent of their $2.3 trillion in reserves in dollars, have had mixed success in checking gains in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Japan has stayed out of the market since March, while the Bank of Korea has issued plenty of verbal warnings but has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively enough to halt the dollar's fall.   \par \par \uc2 "The Bank of Korea has so far been fighting a psychological war," said Jimmy Koh, head of treasury research at Singapore-based United Overseas Bank.   \par \par \uc2 South Korea's reserves jumped $14.2 billion to a record $192.6 billion in November. About $10 billion of the increase could not be explained by current account data, but the apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was outweighed by exporter selling.   \par \par \uc2 Many South Korean exporters panicked after the dollar plunged below their forecast ranges from 1,100 won to 1,060 won, reducing profits below what they had budgeted for in won terms.   \par \par \uc2 "You can't afford to waste too much ammunition when the dollar's plunge is broad-based," Koh said, referring to criticism from South Korean lawmakers that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had misused taxpayers' money in a vain attempt to stall the won's surge.   \par \par \uc2 In Asia, South Korean exporters such as Samsung and Hyundai Motor Co. have borne the brunt of the dollar's fall.   \par \par \uc2 Samsung is the 10th worst-performing stock in the Kospi 200 Index in the past three months.   \par \par \uc2 Analysts say Hyundai Motors would suffer a 1.5 percent fall in its earnings per share next year for every percentage point decline in the dollar against the won. The automaker derives 40 percent of its revenue from dollar-denominated exports.   \par \par \uc2 Samsung and Hyundai were not immediately available to comment.   \par \par \uc2 For sure, the won's gains have helped reduce the cost of imported raw materials and enabled the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cut rates twice since August.   \par \par \uc2 The worry, though, is the won's outperformance against rival \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will make South Korean exports less competitive at a time when local consumer demand is flagging.   \par \par \uc2 The won is Asia's best-performing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year, having gained almost 13 percent since the start of January.   \par \par \uc2 Its 9 percent rise against the dollar since the end of September has outpaced gains by the euro (up 7.2 percent), the yen (up 5.7 percent) and the Taiwan dollar (up 5.2 percent).   \par \par \uc2 DECISIVE \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 For many analysts, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  still holds the key to an effective Asian strategy to halt \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains and protect local exporters.   \par \par \uc2 Tim Condon at ING Bank in Singapore expects Tokyo will repeat the huge dollar buying it mounted in the first quarter to pull the yen down from three-year highs if the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciates on trade-weighted terms to last year's levels.   \par \par \uc2 "The lesson from its successful \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in January was that massive \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  works and can, at least for some time, reverse the rise of the yen," said Condon.   \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be successful and, as before, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will invest the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  proceeds in U.S. Treasuries," he said. ((Editing by Alan Wheatley;rajat.bhattacharya@reuters.com; Reuters Messaging: rajat.bhattacharya.reuters.com@reuters.net; +65 6870 3841)).    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041209e0c90053k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
