\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 :Dlr Up Vs Euro On Europe Warning;Up Vs Yen -2-  \b0\par\par\uc2 285 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 2004\par 21:04\par \uc2 OsterDowJones Commodity Wire\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2004, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  Standard Attribution Statement: News Provided by COMTEX.  \par \par \uc2 Dec 08, 2004 (ODC via COMTEX) --  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the dollar may hold in coming sessions above Y101.22, a low marked on Dec. 23, 1999, said Akifumi Uchida, senior manager of financial products and marketing department at Sumitomo Trust and Banking. That's partly because weak Japanese data recently have increased speculation that officials of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  may order yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the slowing economy. "When (Japanese MOF officials) say they care about economic fundamentals, they mean growth rates, and when you compare the rates of expansion between Japan and the U.S., you can see Japan's fundamentals are clearly weaker," Uchida said. "That means the yen should be weaker ... Japan has the justification of fighting" against a rising home \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . But Uchida thinks in the longer term the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely to break below Y100.00 for the first time in nine years, perhaps early next year, because Japan can't turn the tide of broad dollar-weakness on its own. The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overall downtrend will probably persist barring joint Europe-\b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , something which few players think is in the works for now, he said. However, Societe Generale's Fujita said the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if the euro strengthens dramatically enough. "If $1.3500, $1.3600, $1.3700 all give before the end of the year and $1.4000 looks possible, then I'm sure they'll come in at some point," he said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 Copyright 2004 Dow Jones. All rights reserved.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020041209e0c80006z\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
