\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar rises, investors focus on rates.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Katie Hunt  \par \uc2 685 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 2004\par 12:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 8 (Reuters) - The dollar gained ground on Wednesday, as investors took profits on other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on signs that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength may prompt some central banks to scale back interest rate tightening.  \par \par \uc2 Worries about the United States' ability to fund its huge current account deficit have led to persistent weakness in the dollar, taking it to fresh record lows against the euro on Tuesday and five-year lows against the yen last week.  \par \par \uc2 But investors took profits on the climb of a broad spectrum of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar as decisions by Canada and Australia this week to leave interest rates unchanged sparked concern about the speed of the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves and their effect on economic growth.  \par \par \uc2 "Moderating interest rate expectations combined with the end-of-year dollar profit-taking effect, that's what is pushing the dollar higher," said Adam Myers, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Societe Generale.  \par \par \uc2 "I still think the dollar is a good sell but it looks like the market has got to push the dollar higher a bit before it comes back," he added.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar pierced the $1.33 barrier to this week's high of $1.3294 per euro in early European trade, nearly two cents above record lows of $1.3470 set in the previous session. By 1044 GMT, the dollar stood at $1.3314 per euro, up three quarters of a percent from the U.S. close.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar rose to its highest against the yen in almost three weeks at 103.98 yen, one percent above late New York levels.  \par \par \uc2 Dollar gains were more pronounced against the Australian dollar and the Canadian dollar after the countries' central banks left interest rates unchanged this week and raised concerns about the impact of a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on growth.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar has recovered nearly five percent from recent nine-month lows against the Australian dollar and four percent from 12-year lows against the Canadian dollar, as investors fear the strength of the commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  is starting to damage their economies.  \par \par \uc2 Commodity and oil prices have fallen this week, providing additional support for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , since the United States is the world's largest consumer of oil.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. oil prices touched a new three-month low at $41.37 on Wednesday, $14 below record highs hit in October.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  FOCUS  \par \par \uc2 Comments from euro zone policymakers this week have also made market players cautious about chasing the dollar down to $1.35 per euro, a level at which many traders believe the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would consider taking action.  \par \par \uc2 Concern also remains about Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen. Japanese authorities \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily in the first three months of the year to weaken their \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and make Japanese exports more competitive.  \par \par \uc2 "If we get another sharp move lower in dollar/yen to 100 yen then I don't think there's any doubt that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  would resume its \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said Myers.  \par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, the U.S. is the only major economy expected to raise interest rates this month.  \par \par \uc2 The Fed is widely expected to increase rates by 25 basis points to 2.25 percent next Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said losses in the dollar - which has plunged around nine percent versus the euro and the yen in about two months - were starting to affect global rates.  \par \par \uc2 The Reserve Bank of Australia said on Wednesday that it would keep its official cash rate unchanged at 5.25 percent. The Bank of Canada kept key interest rates steady at 2.50 percent on Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 "Commodity prices are also coming under pressure and people will be pointing to the narrowing interest rate differential behind moves in Canadian and Australian dollars," said Riz Din, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Barclays Capital.  \par \par \uc2 The central banks of Britain, New Zealand and Sweden all meet this week, but all are expected to keep rates steady.  \par \par \uc2 Interest rate differentials were starting to work in favour of the dollar, analysts said, with this week's Treasury auctions of five-and 10-year paper expected to attract demand.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041209e0c8004nq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
