\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar rises, investors focus on rates.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Katie Hunt  \par \uc2 685 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 2004\par 12:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Dec 8 (Reuters) - The dollar gained ground on Wednesday, as investors took profits on other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on signs that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength may prompt some central banks to scale back interest rate tightening.  \par \par \uc2 Worries about the United States' ability to fund its huge current account deficit have led to persistent weakness in the dollar, taking it to fresh record lows against the euro on Tuesday and five-year lows against the yen last week.  \par \par \uc2 But investors took profits on the climb of a broad spectrum of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar as decisions by Canada and Australia this week to leave interest rates unchanged sparked concern about the speed of the recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves and their effect on economic growth.  \par \par \uc2 "Moderating interest rate expectations combined with the end-of-year dollar profit-taking effect, that's what is pushing the dollar higher," said Adam Myers, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Societe Generale.  \par \par \uc2 "I still think the dollar is a good sell but it looks like the market has got to push the dollar higher a bit before it comes back," he added.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar pierced the $1.33 barrier to this week's high of $1.3294 per euro in early European trade, nearly two cents above record lows of $1.3470 set in the previous session. By 1044 GMT, the dollar stood at $1.3314 per euro, up three quarters of a percent from the U.S. close.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar rose to its highest against the yen in almost three weeks at 103.98 yen , one percent above late New York levels.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dollar gains were more pronounced against the Australian dollar  and\par the Canadian dollar        after the countries' central banks left\par interest rates unchanged this week and raised concerns about the impact\par of a strong \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on growth.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar has recovered nearly five percent from recent nine-month lows against the Australian dollar and four percent from 12-year lows against the Canadian dollar, as investors fear the strength of the commodity \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is starting to damage their economies.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Commodity and oil prices have fallen this week, providing additional support for the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , since the United States is the world's largest consumer of oil.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 U.S. oil prices touched a new three-month low at $41.37 on Wednesday, $14 below record highs hit in October.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CENTRAL BANK\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  FOCUS  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Comments from euro zone policymakers this week have also made market players cautious about chasing the dollar down to $1.35 per euro, a level at which many traders believe the European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would consider taking action.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Concern also remains about Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to weaken the yen. Japanese authorities \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  heavily in the first three months of the year to weaken their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and make Japanese exports more competitive.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "If we get another sharp move lower in dollar/yen to 100 yen then I don't think there's any doubt that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would resume its \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," said Myers.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Meanwhile, the U.S. is the only major economy expected to raise interest rates this month.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Fed is widely expected to increase rates by 25 basis points to 2.25 percent next Tuesday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts said losses in the dollar - which has plunged around nine percent versus the euro and the yen in about two months - were starting to affect global rates.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Reserve Bank of Australia said on Wednesday that it would keep its official cash rate unchanged at 5.25 percent. The Bank of Canada kept key interest rates steady at 2.50 percent on Tuesday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Commodity prices are also coming under pressure and people will be pointing to the narrowing interest rate differential behind moves in Canadian and Australian dollars," said Riz Din, \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at Barclays Capital.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The central banks of Britain, New Zealand and Sweden all meet this week, but all are expected to keep rates steady.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Interest rate differentials were starting to work in favour of the dollar, analysts said, with this week's Treasury auctions of five-and 10-year paper expected to attract demand.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041208e0c80073o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
