\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2  VIEW:Weak Dlr Sparks Global  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Headaches  \b0\par\par\uc2 1,020 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Dezember 2004\par 22:08\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    By Laurence Norman \par    A DOW JONES NEWSWIRES COLUMN \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--As European and Japanese officials grab headlines with their statements of concern, pleas for help and angry foot-stamping about the dollar's declines, attention to the conundrums the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's weakness is sparking for other central banks has been somewhat sidelined.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 That may have changed somewhat Tuesday, when the Bank of Canada cited local dollar strength as a potential drag on its economy and therefore a central reason for keeping its benchmark overnight rate at 2.50%.  \par \par \uc2 And Canada isn't alone. From South America to the Far East, the dollar's long bout of decline is adding an extra dimension to the always delicate balancing act that central banks face: keeping economies growing and inflation in-check, while steering clear of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  manipulation.  \par \par \uc2 In explaining its decision to hold rates steady - a move that came to be widely expected in recent days - the Bank of Canada said that while inflation was on track, there was some downside risk to growth because of a strong Canadian dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "The U.S. dollar has depreciated further against major floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , including the Canadian dollar," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement. "If exchange rates were to persist at current levels, and if all other economic and financial factors were to remain unchanged, there would be a dampening effect on aggregate demand for Canadian goods and services."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar had lost around 8.4% year-to-date until Tuesday morning against the Canadian dollar, making the latter one of the year's best performers. By comparison, the euro has gained just 6.3% this year, despite now trading at all-time lows.  \par \par \uc2 Loose monetary policy in the U.S. is seen as at least partly responsible for the dollar's fall. By keeping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  printing presses on, the Federal Reserve has placed cheap dollars in the hands of U.S. consumers, who can spend them on imports and in the hands of businesses and speculators, who can invest them abroad.  \par \par \uc2 Many analysts continue to believe the Bank of Canada will raise rates in the medium-term, as authorities keep the inflationary effects of a growing economy that may be close to capacity in check. But the rate-tightening cycle may be tougher going now. "Judging by the comments on the exchange rate, it almost sounds like rates need to be at stimulative levels to offset the impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , so this is pretty close to neutral," said Doug Porter, senior economist at BMO Nesbitt Burns Inc.  \par \par \uc2 A few thousand miles south, the Colombian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is facing a similar dilemma. The peso had gained around 11% by the end of November in the spot market, despite the bank saying in September it would buy $1 billion by year's end. That's hurting exporters, something President Alvaro Uribe acknowledged in September when he said the country needed a competitive \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate," adding "I dislike the appreciation."  \par \par \uc2 Cutting rates would be an ideal solution and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did that in March, reducing them to 6.75%, but with inflation at the upper end of where the bank wants it, Clyde Wardle, head of emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at HSBC, says that will be tough.  \par \par \uc2 "I think in Colombia there is obviously concern about the strength of the Colombian peso ... They may be interested in cutting rates, but inflation is above where they might want it to be," he said.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Qualms \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Dollar weakness presents a different problem for some Asian countries - more a political complication than an outright economic one. South Korea, for instance, has not only cut interest rates but has once again gone down the controversial \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  road as it attempts to weaken the won, which is trading close to seven-year highs.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 That's politically sensitive at a time when the rest of the world is calling on Asian countries to stop trying to manipulate their \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and insulate them from the effects of the weakening dollar. Even \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the most ardent practitioner of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the industrialized world, hasn't \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the markets since the first quarter.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yet dollar weakness need not always be a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  headache. HSBC's Wardle said Brazil's decision to openly \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to buy dollars and stem the real's appreciation this week doesn't mean it's losing out from the dollar's slide. The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  says it's doing so to build reserves not to target an exchange rate. The government has some $10-$11 billion of interest and principal payments on its foreign debt due next year. Part of that is expected to come from exchange reserves.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Wardle points out that a weaker dollar reduces the country's debt load and helps it deal with high international oil prices. As a deflationary factor, the stronger real may be pushing Brazil toward a time when it can stop raising its reference Selic rate, which now stands at 17.25%.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 And while he admits that some sectors of the economy and the government may fret about the headline exchange rate of the real to the dollar, the Brazilian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is actually "really unchanged" year-to-date against the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of its largest trading partners, noting that Brazil exports more to Europe than it does to the U.S. The result: Brazil can lift its reserves and quieten political complaints via occasional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , while it enjoys the beneficial side-effects of a weaker dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Politicians can have a somewhat distorted viewpoint of the real impact of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," Wardle said. "But there really isn't any justification" for worrying about the strength of the Brazilian real right now.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Laurence Norman covers \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  for Dow Jones Newswires in New York. He has previously covered the Argentine economy for Dow Jones in Buenos Aires.)  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Laurence Norman, Dow Jones Newswires, 1-201-938-2096; laurence.norman@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Don Curren in Toronto contributed to this report.) [ 12-07-04 1608ET ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020041207e0c70003o\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (japan near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Quelle\cell \pard \ql \